这样，他也许不会来了
Well, I guess that's a no.

167
00:10:54,260 --> 00:10:57,560
毕加索就喜欢我们的黑色幽默
Yeah, Uncle Pablo loved it when we joked this way about death.

168
00:10:58,140 --> 00:11:00,380
死亡又是什么？
Yes, but what is death?

169
00:11:01,040 --> 00:11:03,440
太深奥了
Oh, you are so deep.

170
00:11:03,920 --> 00:11:06,660
-有时候吓着我了 -谢谢
- Sometimes it even scares me. - Thank you.

171
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:09,480
能遇到你们的家庭.
You know, it really is extraordinary...

172
00:11:09,480 --> 00:11:12,220
真是太不寻常了
meeting a family like you in a place like this.

173
00:11:12,905 --> 00:11:14,099
- Oh? - Oh?

174
00:11:14,300 --> 00:11:18,860
还以为只有在城里才能享受 这么高雅的夜晚
I mean, I thought I'd have to go into the city to find a cultural evening like this.

175
00:11:18,860 --> 00:11:22,280
因为乡下人都文盲
Because Lord knows that most suburbanites are brain dead.

176
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:26,980
米克，我想起来了.
Which reminds me, Mishka...

177
00:11:29,180 --> 00:11:31,680
你能不能陪我进城.
I was wondering if you'd like to come to the city with me...

178
00:11:31,680 --> 00:11:33,200
去欣赏戏剧艺术
to see some performance art.

179
00:11:35,100 --> 00:11:38,140
麦克，去吧，因为这里乡下地方.
Oh, go, Mike. No, go, go. Because Lord knows...

180
00:11:38,140 --> 00:11:41,220
确实没有戏剧艺术可言
you can't get a decent piece of performance art in the suburbs.

181
00:11:42,560 --> 00:11:44,800
真是迫不及待呢
Yeah, you know, that really burns me up.

182
00:11:45,940 --> 00:11:48,680
明天是哥哈特的最后一场演出
Tomorrow is the last night of Gerhardts performance piece.

183
00:11:48,680 --> 00:11:51,160
我希望你能陪我去看
And there's no one I'd rather see it with than you.

184
00:11:52,600 --> 00:11:53,840
好吧，一言为定
Well, then, it's a date.

185
00:11:54,800 --> 00:11:56,200
-麦克 -怎么了？
- Mike. - Yeah, Mom?

186
00:11:56,800 --> 00:11:58,400
你忘了？
Aren't you forgetting something?

187
00:11:58,400 --> 00:12:01,880
是啊，原来的安排，也是明天晚上
Yeah, a prior commitment, like something else for tomorrow night?

188
00:12:02,760 --> 00:12:07,160
对家庭来说是件重大的事
One that's very, very important to your entire family?

189
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:11,700
明晚并没有什么安排吧
Gee, no, I don't think I had any plans for tomorrow night.

190
00:12:12,420 --> 00:12:14,320
肯定有，我们要.
Sure you do, Mike. We're supposed to go--

191
00:12:17,040 --> 00:12:18,760
米克，他在干什么？
Mishka, what is he doing?

192
00:12:21,220 --> 00:12:21,940
他在跳舞
He's dancing.

193
00:12:22,060 --> 00:12:26,600
匪夷所思的是 这位哲学家也喜欢现代舞蹈
Yes, incredibly enough, little Ben, here, is a philosopher and a modern dancer.

194
00:12:26,707 --> 00:12:29,176
明晚他要表演
Now, he's got a recital tomorrow night...

195
00:12:29,380 --> 00:12:31,320
不过哲学家跳舞嘛.
but once you've seen one little philosopher dance...

196
00:12:31,400 --> 00:12:32,080
都是一个样的
you've seen them all.

197
00:12:33,020 --> 00:12:34,140
那我们说定了
So, we're on?

198
00:12:37,240 --> 00:12:38,560
是的，驷马难追
Right, we're on.

199
00:12:48,740 --> 00:12:50,640
米克，再见
Au revoir, Mishka.

200
00:12:59,160 --> 00:13:01,460
真是有气质
Hey, was she incredible, or what, huh?

201
00:13:02,880 --> 00:13:04,240
我知道.
I know, I know.

202
00:13:04,740 --> 00:13:06,740
很抱歉，我不能出席保龄球赛
Look, I'm sorry I had to pass on the bowling...

203
00:13:06,840 --> 00:13:08,580
你们能体谅我的
but I knew you guys would understand.

204
00:13:10,020 --> 00:13:11,420
不体谅？
You don't understand.

205
00:13:14,400 --> 00:13:16,380
不原谅？
You really don't understand.

206
00:13:18,340 --> 00:13:20,920
麦克，你答应过的，你一定要去
Mike, you have to go with us. You promised.

207
00:13:21,360 --> 00:13:24,260
没有你，我们怎么能打败库斯曼家？
How are we supposed to beat the Koosmans without you?

208
00:13:24,520 --> 00:13:26,500
不就是一场球赛吗？
You guys, it's just a game.

209
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:29,140
问题不在这，你许下了承诺
That's not the point, Mike. You made a commitment.

210
00:13:29,400 --> 00:13:30,560
我们都依靠你了
We're all counting on you.

211
00:13:30,800 --> 00:13:34,300
如果家人都不可靠，还能靠谁？
And if you can't count on your family, who can you count on?

212
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:39,740
爸爸，我交到朋友了
Look, Dad, I'm involved in a relationship here.

213
00:13:39,740 --> 00:13:40,800
而且是艺术家
With an artist.

214
00:13:41,580 --> 00:13:43,960
我怎能放弃机会去打球呢？
I can't just drop that to go bowling.

215
00:13:44,480 --> 00:13:45,800
朋友？
A relationship?

216
00:13:46,340 --> 00:13:50,040
她对你一无所知 她还以为你叫“米克”
She doesn't even know who you are. She thinks you're "Mishka."

217
00:13:50,420 --> 00:13:52,640
其实你和我们一样，打保龄球的
And you're just a bowler like the rest of us.

218
00:13:53,460 --> 00:13:54,700
你怎么知道我会没出息？
Hey, how do you know what I am?

219
00:13:54,700 --> 00:13:58,220
说不定我不是打保龄球的 说不定我就是“米克”
Maybe I'm not a bowler. Maybe I am Mishka.

220
00:13:59,700 --> 00:14:01,240
我快吐了
Maybe I'm gonna barf.

221
00:14:03,280 --> 00:14:06,640
若在旧时代，他早被枪毙了
If this we're the Russian Army, he'd be tried for desertion and shot.

222
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:10,140
凯罗，牛不喝水按不下牛头
Carol, we're not going to force your brother to go bowling with us.

223
00:14:10,380 --> 00:14:14,080
不过我有预感 他很快会意识到自己不是“米克”
Anyway, I have a hunch that pretty soon he'll realize he's not Mishka.

224
00:14:15,360 --> 00:14:17,420
我算什么？我只是个油漆匠
But what do I know? I'm just a painter.

225
00:14:21,700 --> 00:14:22,880
“牛的精髓”
"Essence of Cow? "

226
00:14:24,124 --> 00:14:26,954
-真是杰作 -这个，我很喜爱
- What a piece of-- - This? I love this.

227
00:14:27,100 --> 00:14:29,840
是啊，我也很喜爱
Oh, yes. Yes, I love this thing.

228
00:14:30,063 --> 00:14:33,530
牛我见过，不过没这个牛
I mean, I haven't seen cow essence before, but this....

229
00:14:33,534 --> 00:14:36,602
-安德雷，费比兹奥 -朱丽叶!
- Andre! Fabrizzio! - Oh, Juliet!

230
00:14:41,460 --> 00:14:44,320
哥特勒的画展后，我们还没见过呢
God, I haven't seen you since the Gertrude Stein-a-thon.

231
00:14:45,060 --> 00:14:48,500
这是我的好朋友麦克.西弗 麦克是一名诗人
This is a good friend of mine, Michael Seaver. Michael is a poet.

232
00:14:48,740 --> 00:14:50,780
表演快要开始了
Oh, look, the performance piece is about to start.

233
00:14:51,240 --> 00:14:52,360
听说很棒呢
Oh, I hear it's brilliant.

234
00:15:05,340 --> 00:15:09,040
-猩猩对着阳光.. -在吠叫
- Orangutans bark at the sound of.... - Sunlight.

235
00:15:09,360 --> 00:15:12,680
-为什么没有.. -木材
- Why are there no.... - Lumberjacks....

236
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:15,340
-在城市里？ -大城市
- In big cities? - Big cities.

237
00:15:26,580 --> 00:15:28,420
太棒了!精彩!
Brilliant! Absolutely brilliant!

238
00:15:28,600 --> 00:15:30,100
这是对美国中产阶级的时尚 和缺陷的.
It's a perfect commentary...

239
00:15:30,100 --> 00:15:32,620
最好的抨击
on the fashions and foibles of middle-class America.

240
00:15:32,860 --> 00:15:34,680
是的，当然是的
Oh, yes, yes, absolutely.

241
00:15:36,100 --> 00:15:36,940
时尚还有缺陷
Fashions and foibles.

242
00:15:38,900 --> 00:15:40,380
米克，说笑吧？
Oh, Mishka, you can't be serious.

243
00:15:40,460 --> 00:15:42,960
这显然是对解除核子武器的呼吁
I mean, it's obviously a plea for nuclear disarmament.

244
00:15:44,080 --> 00:15:46,607
显然是解除核子武器
Obviously. Yes, nuclear disarmament.

245
00:15:46,607 --> 00:15:49,260
这都看不出来就真是傻瓜了
You'd have to be dumb as a post to miss that.

246
00:15:49,260 --> 00:15:54,040
那么这是对时尚.
So you're saying it's a comment on contemporary fashions...

247
00:15:54,040 --> 00:15:55,660
还有对核武器的抨击？
and nuclear disarmament?

248
00:15:56,180 --> 00:15:58,120
对，是的
Yes. Yes, right.

249
00:15:58,800 --> 00:16:01,960
对，大家都知道，现在的时尚是.
I mean, everybody knows that contemporary fashions are...

250
00:16:01,960 --> 00:16:03,480
核子武器
obviously nuclear.

251
00:16:04,280 --> 00:16:05,680
所以要解除
And that's disarming.

252
00:16:09,960 --> 00:16:12,320
好了，队员们，出发!
All right, team, et's go!

253
00:16:13,840 --> 00:16:14,201
-一起喊“S”!
-“S” - Give me an "S"! - "S."

254
00:16:14,201 --> 00:16:16,641
-一起喊“E!”
-“E” - Give me an "E"! - "E."

255
00:16:17,880 --> 00:16:19,640
好吧，我自己来
All right, I'll finish it myself.

256
00:16:20,240 --> 00:16:23,860
-“AVER!”什么单词？ -“输定了”!
- A-V-E-R! What does it spell? - Losers.

257
00:16:25,340 --> 00:16:29,149
拜托，虽然主力队员不在.
No, come on. Now, maybe we've lost one of our stronger team members...

258
00:16:29,149 --> 00:16:31,500
但我们相信还是会赢
but we've gotta believe we're gonna win.

259
00:16:31,500 --> 00:16:35,620
为什么相信我们会赢？
And we do believe we're gonna win. And why do we believe we're gonna win?

260
00:16:36,260 --> 00:16:37,400
因为我们是白痴
Because we're idiots?

261
00:16:39,380 --> 00:16:41,600
不，因为我们是.
No, Ben. Because we're...

262
00:16:42,800 --> 00:16:44,320
“西弗保龄球队”!
"The Bowlin Seavers."

263
00:16:45,799 --> 00:16:47,801
怎么看？瞧瞧
What do you think? Look at this.

264
00:16:47,801 --> 00:16:51,765
-“西弗高人”？ -还不止呢
- "Jason "Bud" Seaver"? - And that's not all.

265
00:16:52,220 --> 00:16:54,608
还有一件.
I also have one here...

266
00:16:54,608 --> 00:16:57,708
“西弗牛人”
for Ben "Fudd" Seaver.

267
00:16:58,545 --> 00:17:01,849
还有“西弗迷人”
For Carol "Spud" Seaver.

268
00:17:02,149 --> 00:17:03,650
好玩吧？
Isn't this fun?

269
00:17:03,650 --> 00:17:06,553
还有你的“西弗狂人”
And Maggie "Mud" Seaver.

270
00:17:06,553 --> 00:17:08,253
“狂人”？
Mud?

271
00:17:08,560 --> 00:17:11,000
我再也想不出什么花哨词儿了
Well, there aren't that many words that end in "ud."

272
00:17:12,860 --> 00:17:14,094
准备好没？
Okay, we ready?

273
00:17:14,094 --> 00:17:16,129
-一起喊“S”!
-“S”! - Now, give me an "S"! - "S! "

274
00:17:16,129 --> 00:17:17,531
-一起喊“E”!
-“E”! - Give me an "E"! - "E! "

275
00:17:17,531 --> 00:17:18,665
-一起喊“A”!
-“A”! - Give me an "A"! - "A! "

276
00:17:18,665 --> 00:17:19,766
-一起喊“V”!
-“V”! - Give me a "V"! - "V! "

277
00:17:19,766 --> 00:17:20,934
-一起喊“E”!
-“E”! - Give me an "E"! - "E! "

278
00:17:20,934 --> 00:17:22,497
-一起喊“R”!
-“R”! - Give me an "R"! - "R! "

279
00:17:22,680 --> 00:17:24,500
-什么单词？ -“输定了”!
- What do you got? - Losers!

280
00:17:27,300 --> 00:17:29,440
麦克，说说你的作品吧
So, Michael, why don't we talk about your work?

281
00:17:29,520 --> 00:17:32,160
麦克那天念了一首很棒的诗
Michael read the most remarkable poem the other day.

282
00:17:32,800 --> 00:17:36,520
这只是我最近学习新象征主义的作品
It was just a little something from my recent neo-symbolist period.

283
00:17:36,780 --> 00:17:39,280
是吗？之前你是什么流派的？
Really? What we're you before you became a neo-symbolist?

284
00:17:42,020 --> 00:17:42,820
之前是.
I was...

285
00:17:43,991 --> 00:17:45,929
新橡皮主义!
a Neo-Synephrine!

286
00:17:48,180 --> 00:17:50,560
他是说笑!真有意思!
Oh, a joke! How funny!

287
00:17:52,420 --> 00:17:55,720
麦克，现在就朗诵一首诗吧!
Well, Michael, why don't you read one of your poems for us now?

288
00:17:55,900 --> 00:17:57,460
立刻来
Yes, now. Right now.

289
00:17:58,100 --> 00:18:00,940
大家好，我要介绍麦克.西弗 优秀的.
Everybody, I'd like to introduce Michael Seaver. An exciting--

290
00:18:00,940 --> 00:18:04,020
-不行 -为什么？
- Juliet, I can't do that. - Why not?

291
00:18:04,100 --> 00:18:05,220
稿子没带来
I didn't even bring my poem.

292
00:18:06,020 --> 00:18:08,280
那又怎样？以前的作品随便来一首
So what? Why don't you recite one of your older works?

293
00:18:09,140 --> 00:18:10,600
我实在朗诵不出来
No, actually, I couldn't do that.

294
00:18:11,420 --> 00:18:12,700
麦克，这什么意思？
What are you talking about, Michael?

295
00:18:14,180 --> 00:18:15,840
朱丽叶，这是法律问题
Look, Juliet, it's this legal thing.

296
00:18:16,120 --> 00:18:18,780
我把诗歌都卖给好莱坞了
I mean, I sold all my poems to Hollywood...

297
00:18:18,840 --> 00:18:21,060
现在只有杰克.尼科尔森才有权朗读
and from now on only Jack Nicholsons allowed to read them.

298
00:18:21,320 --> 00:18:23,940
米克，你就别打趣了 快来一首
Oh, Mishka, stop joking around and read your poem.

299
00:18:24,940 --> 00:18:27,300
-大家都在等 -朱丽叶.
- Everybody's waiting. - Look, look, Juliet.

300
00:18:27,380 --> 00:18:30,240
-我有话要说 -什么？
- I have to tell you something. - What?

301
00:18:33,740 --> 00:18:37,200
-老实说我不是诗人 -什么？
- The truth is, I'm not a poet. - What?

302
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:41,940
-那你念的诗..？ -不是我写的，买来的
- But the poem you read, it was-- - I didn't write it. I bought it.

303
00:18:45,020 --> 00:18:47,020
你是说你骗了我？
You mean you lied to me?

304
00:18:47,700 --> 00:18:51,340
朱丽叶，你一走进教室.
Look, Juliet, when you first walked into that classroom...

305
00:18:52,600 --> 00:18:55,640
我就知道你兴众不同
I thought you we're so much different, so much classier...

306
00:18:55,640 --> 00:18:58,840
比任何人都更高贵，我只是想讨好你
than anyone else I'd ever seen. I just wanted to impress you.

307
00:18:59,560 --> 00:19:02,636
但你家人，普利策文学奖，现代舞蹈.
But your family, the Pulitzer Prize, the modern dance recital--

308
00:19:02,636 --> 00:19:06,060
我家里人并不是什么现代舞者
No, no. My family's not at a modern dance recital.

309
00:19:06,060 --> 00:19:08,260
-那这是干嘛？ -保龄球!
- Then what was this? - Bowling!

310
00:19:10,400 --> 00:19:13,020
-保龄球 -对了，保龄球
- Bowling. - Yeah, bowling.

311
00:19:13,620 --> 00:19:16,160
这是我们和邻居一年一度的比赛
See, it's this big match we have every year with the neighbors.

312
00:19:16,240 --> 00:19:18,160
叫做“保龄球大餐比赛”
It's called "Bowling for Dinners."

313
00:19:18,500 --> 00:19:19,600
这是我爸的主意
That was my dad's idea.

314
00:19:20,020 --> 00:19:21,340
谁输了.
And the losers have to take the winners out...

315
00:19:21,340 --> 00:19:24,480
就要到费博餐厅请吃一顿大鱼大肉
for a big surf 'n' turf dinner at Ferber's House of Meat and Fish.

316
00:19:26,600 --> 00:19:29,420
费博餐厅，大鱼大肉？
Ferber's House of Meat and Fish?

317
00:19:30,730 --> 00:19:34,396
-什么？ -真恶心
- What? - Well, it's such a disgusting image.

318
00:19:34,460 --> 00:19:37,720
两家人打保龄球争肉吃
I mean, two entire families rolling balls for meat.

319
00:19:39,005 --> 00:19:43,444
还有蔬菜，米饭和马铃薯!
Hey, it comes with a salad and choice of rice or potato, okay?

320
00:19:43,620 --> 00:19:44,940
真不敢相信
I don't believe this.

321
00:19:45,340 --> 00:19:47,880
你是打保龄球的.
You're one of those people who bowls...

322
00:19:47,880 --> 00:19:50,380
逛商店的.
and hangs out at malls...

323
00:19:50,380 --> 00:19:53,660
吃热狗的土包子
and eats hot dogs on a stick.

324
00:19:54,780 --> 00:19:56,920
我就是这样，有什么不好？
Yeah, I guess I am. So what's wrong with that?

325
00:19:56,920 --> 00:19:59,620
我喜欢逛商店，喜欢保龄球
Maybe I like malls. Maybe I like bowling.

326
00:20:00,420 --> 00:20:03,296
-麦克，小声点 -干嘛了？我很丢脸是吧？
- Michael, will you please lower your voice. - What? Are you ashamed of me, Juliet?

327
00:20:03,296 --> 00:20:06,080
我让你丢脸了？
You ashamed of being seen here with me?

328
00:20:06,080 --> 00:20:07,560
真是难为情
This is really embarrassing.

329
00:20:07,920 --> 00:20:10,060
丢脸？我教你丢脸？
Oh, you want embarrassing? I'll give you embarrassing.

330
00:20:11,204 --> 00:20:16,108
老兄，想知道大城市里 为什么没有木材吗？
Hey, buddy, you want to know why theres no lumberjacks in the big cities?

331
00:20:16,760 --> 00:20:19,260
因为木材都被削成热狗棍子了
It's because they're all at the malls eating hot dogs on sticks!

332
00:20:32,880 --> 00:20:35,900
-完了 -死定了
- It's over. - We're dead.

333
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:37,700
前途渺茫
It's hopeless.

334
00:20:38,380 --> 00:20:40,840
这么泄气，才输了两场
Now come on, guys, we've only lost two games!

335
00:20:41,600 --> 00:20:43,560
一共才打了两场
We've only played two games.

336
00:20:44,171 --> 00:20:46,639
恨死库斯曼一家了
I hate the Koosmans.

337
00:20:46,880 --> 00:20:49,960
听到了吗，他们已经在吧台唱到.
Did you hear them over there? They had the whole snack bar singing:

338
00:20:50,420 --> 00:20:51,700
★“西弗老弟，名誉扫地”
"We're mopping the floor with the Seaver Four."

339
00:20:53,600 --> 00:20:56,800
连上厕所都这么唱
I won't even tell you what they have them singing in the men's room.

340
00:20:58,260 --> 00:20:59,886
咱练习练习，可以做到的
Well, then, et's practice. Come on, Carol, you can do it.

341
00:20:59,886 --> 00:21:04,084
拿起球，练练出球
et's just grab a ball right now, work on your approach a little bit.

342
00:21:04,140 --> 00:21:06,780
记住绷紧肩膀，臀部和手腕.
Just remember to square your shoulders and whip that wrist...

343
00:21:06,780 --> 00:21:08,240
接着送出去，加油!
and follow through. Okay? Come on.

344
00:21:13,934 --> 00:21:17,698
-打到8分! -对了
- I got eight pins! - Yes.

345
00:21:18,060 --> 00:21:20,360
按规则来说.
Well, I'll have to check the rule book on this...

346
00:21:20,420 --> 00:21:22,580
打到别人的道上没分
but I'm pretty sure they have to be in our lane.

347
00:21:25,940 --> 00:21:29,220
这一顿可要破费了
Well, this will be an expensive dinner this year.

348
00:21:29,680 --> 00:21:31,320
库斯曼一家决定不减肥了
The Koosmans are off their diet.

349
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:33,680
该死的
The slobs.

350
00:21:45,832 --> 00:21:48,635
对不起，我迟到了
Hi, guys. Sorry, I'm late.

351
00:21:48,635 --> 00:21:50,703
麦克
Mike.

352
00:21:54,240 --> 00:21:56,440
关于我的所作所为.
Hey, look, guys, about the way I've been acting....

353
00:21:59,100 --> 00:22:00,940
不知道该怎么说了
I don't know how to say this, but....

354
00:22:02,280 --> 00:22:04,660
-我欠大家一个道歉 -麦克
- Well, I guess I owe you guys.... - Hey, Mike.

355
00:22:06,720 --> 00:22:07,420
爸爸
Yeah, Dad.

356
00:22:09,300 --> 00:22:11,680
要打球还是要写诗？
Do you want to bowl or are you gonna write a poem about it?

357
00:22:14,320 --> 00:22:15,360
我要打球
I'm gonna bowl.

358
00:22:16,540 --> 00:22:19,800
那就赶快练习
And you better hurry, too. Better bowl fast, Michael.

359
00:22:20,960 --> 00:22:23,180
好的，来了
All right, here we go.

360
00:22:28,608 --> 00:22:31,348
米克!
Hey, Mishka!

361
00:22:36,660 --> 00:22:38,640
★我们得第一!
We're number one! Yes!

362
00:22:44,880 --> 00:22:46,860
大家听好了.
All right, all right, attention, please.

363
00:22:47,260 --> 00:22:49,400
我现在代表西弗全家.
On behalf of the entire Seaver family...

364
00:22:49,460 --> 00:22:53,060
我代表“牛人”，“狂人”，“迷人” “强人”和我本人“高人”.
I'm talking about Fudd, Spud, Mud, and of course myself, Bud...

365
00:22:54,140 --> 00:22:56,760
把这个颁发给使我们胜利的人
may I present this to the man who led us to victory.

366
00:23:01,580 --> 00:23:05,211
我看还是家里人对我最了解
Well, I guess when all's said and done, it's your family who knows you best.

367
00:23:05,211 --> 00:23:09,349
“超人”西弗
"Mike 'Stud' Seaver."

368
00:23:54,900 --> 00:23:55,889
